<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Machilipatnam</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Masulipatnam</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Machilipatnam, historically Masulipatnam, is a port town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> delta in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Under the Golconda Sultanate it was the main outlet for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coromandel-coast">Coromandel</a> textiles, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> (1605), English (1611) and French set up factories there. The British took it from the French in 1759, and the town is known for its kalamkari printed cloth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/machilipatnam.jpg" alt="Machilipatnam" width="320" height="151" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Satyach73 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robertson_Square.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
